.TH NVDA-RDP-CLIENT 1 2026-11-22 "nvda-rdp-linux 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvda-rdp-client \- speak and braille a remote Windows NVDA in an RDP session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvda-rdp-client
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvda-rdp-client
is the Linux side of RDAccess, the NVDA add-on that sends the speech and
braille of a remote NVDA screen reader over the dynamic virtual channels
.B NVDA-SPEECH
and
.B NVDA-BRAILLE
of an RDP connection.
.PP
An RDP client built on FreeRDP 3, such as
.BR xfreerdp3 (1)
or
.BR remmina (1),
loads the
.B nvda-rdp-dvc
plugin, which passes both channels to
.B nvda-rdp-client
through two Unix sockets.
.B nvda-rdp-client
speaks through Speech Dispatcher, plays NVDA's tones and sounds through
PipeWire, and shows the braille on the local display through BRLTTY while the
RDP window has the focus. The keys of the braille display go back to the
remote NVDA.
.PP
One process serves both channels and every RDP connection, one after the
other. It is meant to run for the whole graphical session, as the systemd user
service
.BR nvda-rdp-client.service .
If Speech Dispatcher cannot be reached at start, speech is disabled and
braille keeps working; BRLTTY is retried every 5 seconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
Logging level:
.BR DEBUG ,
.BR INFO ,
.B WARNING
or
.BR ERROR .
Default:
.BR INFO .
.TP
.BI \-\-language " LANGUAGE"
Language of the voice and of the connection messages, for example
.BR fr_FR .
It is also reported to the remote NVDA as the language of the local
synthesizer. Default: from
.BR LC_ALL ,
.B LC_MESSAGES
or
.BR LANG ,
else
.BR en .
.TP
.BI \-\-notify " MODE"
Announce connections and disconnections:
.BR none ,
.B message
(spoken, and shown in braille when a display is connected),
.B sound
or
.BR both .
Default:
.BR message .
.TP
.BI \-\-nvda\-waves\-dir " DIRECTORY"
Directory holding a copy of NVDA's
.B waves
directory, from which NVDA's sounds are played. Only files inside it are
played. Default:
.BR $NVDA_WAVES_DIR .
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-player " COMMAND"
Program that plays a WAV file given on its standard input. Default:
.BR "pw\-play \-" .
.SS Speech
.TP
.B \-\-no\-speech
Do not handle the
.B NVDA-SPEECH
channel.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " RATE"
Speech rate on Orca's 0 to 100 scale. Default: 75.
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-module " MODULE"
Speech Dispatcher output module. Default:
.BR espeak\-ng .
.TP
.BI \-\-pitch\-change " OFFSET"
Pitch offset applied to remote speech, as RDAccess's "incoming speech pitch
change"; 0 disables it. Default: 10.
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-pause
Honour NVDA's pause requests. Off by default: the espeak-ng module of Speech
Dispatcher repeated the sentence when speech resumed.
.TP
.B \-\-settings\-management
Let the remote NVDA read and change the local voice, rate, pitch and volume
(RDAccess's "driver settings management"). Off by default.
.SS Braille
.TP
.B \-\-no\-braille
Do not handle the
.B NVDA-BRAILLE
channel.
.TP
.B \-\-braille\-capture
Only log the braille cells; do not use BrlAPI.
.TP
.BI \-\-cells " N" "\fR, \fP" \-\-rows " N"
Display size reported to the remote NVDA until BRLTTY gives the real one.
Default: 40 cells, 1 row.
.TP
.BI \-\-brlapi\-priority " N"
BrlAPI priority, from 1 to 100, while the RDP window has the focus. Default:
60.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-braille\-input
Do not send the keys of the braille display to the remote NVDA.
.TP
.BI \-\-focus\-application " NAME"
Name of the window or application of the RDP client: the remote braille is
shown while a window whose name contains
.I NAME
has the focus. Repeatable. Default:
.B freerdp
and
.BR remmina .
.TP
.B \-\-sync\-caps\-lock
Align the local Caps Lock with the remote NVDA's when the RDP window loses the
focus. It uses the X11 tools
.BR xdotool (1)
and
.BR xset (1),
and may not work under Wayland.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NVDA_WAVES_DIR
Default of
.BR \-\-nvda\-waves\-dir .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory of the sockets shared with the plugin; the RDP client must run with
the same value.
.TP
.BR NVDA_RDP_SOCKET ", " NVDA_RDP_BRAILLE_SOCKET
Paths of the speech and braille sockets, instead of the default ones. The
plugin reads the same variables.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Default language.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nvda-rdp-linux/speech.sock
.TQ
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nvda-rdp-linux/braille.sock
Sockets the plugin connects to; their directory has mode 0700 and the
sockets 0600.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/nvda-rdp-client.service
The user service.
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvda-rdp-linux/environment
Optional settings of the service, one
.IB NAME = value
per line:
.B NVDA_WAVES_DIR
and
.BR NVDA_RDP_OPTIONS ,
the options given to
.BR nvda-rdp-client .
Restart the service after changing it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start the service now and at each graphical login:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now nvda\-rdp\-client.service
.fi
.RE
.PP
Connect with xfreerdp3 (xfreerdp on NixOS), which asks for the password:
.PP
.RS
.nf
xfreerdp3 /v:HOST /u:USER /dvc:nvda\-rdp\-dvc /sound:sys:pulse +f
.fi
.RE
.PP
In Remmina, set "Dynamic virtual channel" to
.B nvda-rdp-dvc
in the advanced settings of the RDP connection.
.PP
Let the remote NVDA change the local voice, and play NVDA's sounds, with the
file
.IR ~/.config/nvda-rdp-linux/environment :
.PP
.RS
.nf
NVDA_WAVES_DIR=/home/user/nvda\-waves
NVDA_RDP_OPTIONS=\-\-settings\-management
.fi
.RE
.PP
Follow the log of the service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
journalctl \-\-user \-u nvda\-rdp\-client \-f
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
The speech and braille that pass through the client are what the remote
screen reader presents, documents and typed text included. The log contains
the spoken text and the braille cells at the
.B INFO
and
.B DEBUG
levels; keep it private.
.PP
RDAccess 1.x is not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvda\-rdp\-server (7),
.BR xfreerdp3 (1),
.BR remmina (1),
.BR speech\-dispatcher (1),
.BR brltty (1)
.PP
https://github.com/pcressant/nvda\-rdp\-linux
